      "sourceTextSha256": "aab7a643d7e012486b3ab7981d2c7596634ec759fca3d0e4d5bc5303111616f0",
      "text": "Day 3 · After breakfast, a tour through the city to the station, where an eco-friendly train climbs through the Tijuca Forest, home to monkeys, exotic animals and birds, to the top of Corcovado. At 710 metres above sea level stands the symbol of Rio, the 38-metre statue of Christ the Redeemer, built in 1931, with a breathtaking panorama of the Rio–Niterói Bridge, Guanabara Bay, the Botanical Garden, the legendary Maracanã Stadium and Sugar Loaf.",
